---
description: USE WHEN generating interactive component examples or documentation to ensure WCAG compliance and accessible Pattern Lab previews.
globs: ["apps/docs/**/*.tsx", "packages/ui/src/patterns/**/*.tsx"]
alwaysApply: false
---
Accessibility Documentation Standards
1. Required Attributes
ARIA: All component examples MUST include appropriate aria-label, aria-expanded, or role attributes as defined by the component's purpose.

Images: Ensure all next/image instances have descriptive alt text or alt="" for decorative elements.

2. Interactive Navigation
Keyboard Access: Documentation examples must be navigable via keyboard. Ensure tabIndex="0" is applied to custom interactive elements.

Event Handlers: Every onClick must have a corresponding onKeyDown or onKeyUp handler for Tab/Space/Enter support.

3. Visual Compliance
Contrast: Previews must adhere to WCAG AA targets (minimum 4.5:1 ratio for standard text).

Focus Indicators: Never disable default focus outlines without providing a high-visibility "Futurist Carton" replacement.
